    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Exploratory Data Analysis (EDA) — Findings\n",
        "\n",
        "## 1. Dataset Overview\n",
        "The original Online Retail dataset contains 541,909 rows and 8 columns. After removing duplicate rows, 536,641 rows remained. A filtered sales dataset containing 524,878 rows and 9 columns was created for sales analysis.\n",
        "\n",
        "## 2. Missing Values\n",
        "- Description: 1,454 missing values (0.27%).\n",
        "- CustomerID: 135,037 missing values (25.16%).\n",
        "- The other columns contained no missing values after duplicate removal.\n",
        "\n",
        "Missing CustomerID values limit customer-level analysis. Such records should be treated as customers with unknown identities rather than assigned fabricated IDs.\n",
        "\n",
        "## 3. Descriptive Statistics and Data Quality\n",
        "Quantity and UnitPrice contained negative and extreme values. The cleaned dataset had 10,587 rows with negative quantities, 2,512 rows with non-positive unit prices, and 9,251 rows with invoice numbers beginning with C. These categories may overlap.\n",
        "\n",
        "## 4. Sales Filtering\n",
        "For the filtered sales analysis, invoice numbers beginning with C were excluded, and only records with positive quantities and positive unit prices were retained. Revenue was calculated as Quantity × UnitPrice.\n",
        "\n",
        "## 5. Visual Analysis\n",
        "- Monthly Revenue Trend: Used to examine revenue changes over time.\n",
        "- Top 10 Products by Revenue: Used to identify products generating the highest revenue.\n",
        "- Top 10 Countries by Revenue: Used to compare revenue contributions across countries.\n",
        "\n",
        "## 6. Conclusion\n",
        "EDA helped identify missing customer information, unusual transaction values, and duplicate records before sales analysis. The filtered dataset was then used to explore monthly revenue, top-performing products, and country-level revenue, supporting the development of the Retail Pulse Analytics Power BI dashboard."
